 "notes": "3 sheets (Views A, B, C), all checked. Units: note 5 'UNITS: INCHES'; values recorded as printed (.562 -> 0.562). Notes 1-5 (sheet 1, text) recorded one entry each (note 1 has blanks 'CAD MODEL ___________ REV. __'; note 3 'APPLICABLE STANDARDS:' with the two ASME lines; note 4 starts with a profile-of-a-surface frame '.05 A B C' drawn as a box, then 'APPLIES TO ALL UNTOLERANCED SURFACES.' - recorded as note, as tolerance.general and as a gdt.frame). Not notes: 'View Rotated 45°' (sheet 3 view label), 'Feature and Specification Index nist_ftc_06_asme1_rd_fsi.pdf' (sheet 1 reference box), captions. GD&T not complete because of datum TARGETS on sheet 3 (J1, J2, K1, K2, G1, H1 - not recorded as gdt.datum). Two-row frames with one symbol cell (profile .02 A B C over flatness .01 on datum D/E; profile .05 D B C over .01 D) are recorded as two frames each (the .05/.01 profile pairs are composite profile frames). Sheet 1 callouts: '2X CR.50 ±.02' (controlled radius), '24X R.125 ±.020', '(SR.500)' reference spherical radius, '2X SØ1.250 ±.008' spherical diameter with position 'SØ.025 D B C' (spherical zone, diameterZone not set), '2X Ø.562 ±.008' position Ø.015 C A B, '2X (cbore) Ø.812 ±.020 (depth) .56 ±.02' position Ø.025(M) C A B (cbore diameter recorded as a dimension with count 2, depth as linear), '4X Ø.415 ±.008 / (cbore) Ø.625 ±.020 (depth) .50 ±.02' position Ø.025(M) A B C, '4X Ø.281 ±.008' position Ø.015 E A B, '(cbore) Ø.40 ±.01 (depth) .31 ±.02' position Ø.02(M) F with '4X INDIVIDUALLY' (datum F also carries '4X INDIVIDUALLY'). Sheet 2: '12.00 ±.01' with perpendicularity .012 A on datum B; perpendicularity .012 A B on datum C; taper '2X 1.00 : 3.00' (conical taper symbol) and slope '1.00 : 2.00' are ratios, NOT recorded as dimensions. Sheet 3: two '.500 ±.008' slot widths with position .025 D C J / .025 D C K (no Ø); '(1.106)' x2 and '(Ø1.000)' x2 reference; 'Ø.250 ±.008 (depth) .50 ±.05' x2 with position Ø.015 D G / Ø.015 D H (hole depth recorded as a separate linear dimension, not inside the hole row). tolerance.tightest: band .016 (±.008, on several sizes - nominal not pinned). Naming rule used for Ø callouts: a callout with an 'nX' count, THRU / depth, or an uppercase (hole) fit is recorded as hole.diameter {diameter, count, upper, lower}; any other Ø size is a dimension {type:'diameter'}. Tolerances are recorded as signed deviations upper/lower; limit dimensions as max/min. GD&T: characteristic in words, datums = the datum letters in order (datum-reference modifiers not encoded), modifiers 'MMC' / 'LMC' = circled M / L after the tolerance value, diameterZone true only where Ø precedes the tolerance."
